docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T68.md:36:2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` exposing: (a) `ReportInput { current: Vec<MetricValue>, baseline: Option<Vec<MetricValue>>, benchmark_report_path: PathBuf, scope: MetricScope, success_criteria: SuccessCriteriaThresholds }`; (b) `RegressionReport` rendering per-signal current value, baseline value, delta, target threshold (from spec §Measurable Success Criteria), pass/fail per row; (c) renderers for human-readable text, machine-readable JSON, and a CI-friendly summary line; (d) per-signal evidence pointer back to the contributing event/memory IDs so any regression is investigable. `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` encodes the spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly (30%, 40%, 80%, 0, 0, 90%) so the report's pass/fail column is grounded in the spec.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T68.md:37:3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` as the CLI binary. Argument surface: `--scope`, `--time-range`, `--signals`, `--baseline <path>`, `--benchmark <path>`, `--format text|json|ci-summary`, `--output <path>`, `--fail-on-regression`. The binary loads the current metrics via the T65 collector against the active workspace, optionally loads a baseline JSON, optionally loads the T66 benchmark JSON, and renders the `RegressionReport` to stdout or the `--output` path. With `--fail-on-regression`, exits non-zero when any signal fails its spec §Measurable Success Criteria target.
