docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md:12:This task creates the canonical metrics module that collects every assistant-usefulness signal required by spec §Phase 9. Without a single module owning these signals, downstream tasks (T66 benchmark fixtures, T67 MCP surface, T68 CLI report, T69 regression tests) would each invent their own definitions and diverge. The module turns the event log + memory access history + workflow outcomes into the nine required signals named in spec §Phase 9: tool calls per successful task, irrelevant files opened per task, relevant anchor recall, memory inclusion precision, memory later-used rate, stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate, tests recommended versus tests needed, and workflow success after first plan.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md:18:> "Phase 9 Deliverables: retrieval relevance metrics; memory usefulness metrics; context token efficiency metrics; stale/contradicted memory surfacing metrics; test-pass-after-plan metrics; repeated-failure reduction metrics; benchmark tasks with golden expected anchors; regression dashboard or CLI report."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md:38:3. In `metrics/signals.rs`, define `pub enum MetricSignal` with one variant per spec-required signal: `ToolCallsPerSuccessfulTask`, `IrrelevantFilesOpenedPerTask`, `RelevantAnchorRecall`, `MemoryInclusionPrecision`, `MemoryLaterUsedRate`, `StaleMemorySurfacedRate`, `ContradictionMissedRate`, `TestsRecommendedVsNeeded`, `WorkflowSuccessAfterFirstPlan`. Derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Hash`. Implement `MetricSignal::as_str()` returning the canonical snake_case wire name used by the T67 MCP surface and the T68 CLI report.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md:70:- Schema parity: `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricSource`, `MetricScope` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; every public field has a doc comment; wire names match the strings used by T67/T68.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T65.md:83:- [ ] No deferred work: every one of the nine spec §Phase 9 "Required metrics" signals is collected by this task — no signal is punted to T67 or T68.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md:1:# T04 — Phase 0 — Baseline benchmark capture (current Lattice workflows)
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md:12:This task captures benchmark numbers for the existing Lattice workflow tools so Phase 4 (retrieval), Phase 9 (metrics), and the hot-path budget assertions in Phase 1 and Phase 2 have a real baseline to regress against. Spec §Phase 0 Deliverables explicitly requires "baseline benchmark suite from current Lattice workflows." Without these numbers, later claims of "no regression" or "30 percent fewer discovery tool calls" cannot be evaluated objectively. The benchmark must follow Rust criterion conventions, run from `cargo bench`, and emit a JSON metrics file the build harness can verify.
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md:16:> "Phase 0 Deliverables: ... baseline benchmark suite from current Lattice workflows."
docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T04.md:20:> Spec §Measurable Success Criteria targets ("30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads") only make sense against a measured baseline.
